{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST expose:\n\n```text\nfinish_search({ search_id: UUID, used: Array<String> })\n    -> { search_id: UUID, finished: true }\n```\n\nThe arguments MUST contain exactly these fields.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.finish_search`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. The harness exposes a `finish_search` tool taking `search_id` (a UUID) and `used` (an array of strings).\n2. The arguments contain exactly those two fields.\n3. The result is `{search_id, finished: true}`.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Exposure and schema.** `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[finish_search_advertises_the_accounting_schema_and_selection_rule]` finds the `finish_search` tool in `definitions()`. It asserts the exact parameter schema:\n  - `search_id` is a string with format uuid.\n  - `used` is an array of strings.\n  - Both fields are required.\n  - `additionalProperties` is false.\n- **Exactly these fields.** `src/authoring/searches.rs#mod[tests]/fn[invalid_completion_is_atomic_and_can_be_corrected]` rejects these argument shapes with an \"exactly search_id and used\" error:\n  - null, an array, and `{}`;\n  - an object missing `used`;\n  - an object missing `search_id`;\n  - an object with an extra field.\n\n  It also rejects:\n  - a non-string or malformed `search_id`;\n  - a `used` value that is not an array;\n  - a `used` array containing a non-string.\n\n  After each rejection it checks that the search is still outstanding and that no inputs were recorded.\n- **Result shape.** `delivered_searches_including_empty_results_need_explicit_completion` and `selected_dependencies_keep_the_delivered_hash_and_accumulate_without_reads` both assert that the result equals `{\"search_id\": <id>, \"finished\": true}`. The second also asserts that there is no `text` field.\n- **Routing.** `src/authoring/tools.rs#fn[dispatch_paged]` routes the `\"finish_search\"` name to `pages.finish_search`. The tests call `pages.finish_search` directly rather than through `dispatch_paged`. That route is a pass-through with no conditional, so it needs no separate test. Other tests in `src/authoring/mod.rs`, such as the conversation tests that count `finish_search` tool calls, also exercise it end to end.\n\n**Conclusion**\nEvery obligation in the requirement text is exercised and asserted. The refining sub-requirements (`completion`, `inputs`, `invalid` and the others) carry their own tests and are outside this assessment. I found no adequacy gap and no marking gap.",
